ead saying  quote we can't just rip up contracts in  contrast labour are against it want to  stop it completely where is nicolas  sturgeon this is taking place in  scotland she  is of course the first minister of that  country today she's written to boris  johnson as you say but merely saying  that he should reassess  that license and licenses in  similar situations now some accuser of  fence sitting certainly greenpeace are  unhappy saying she's deferring to the  prime minister this is a pr exercise but  others in the oil and gas industry in  scotland point out that it employs huge  numbers of people that hydrocarbons are  going to be necessary in the coming  decades and if you don't produce it here  and  employ people in scotland it will mean  importing it from other countries and  their economy is benefiting not ours  meanwhile the chancellor sunak has been  talking about the environment and  balancing uh the health of the planet  and the health of the uk economy this is  what he told sky news earlier look at  our track record over the past a couple  of decades we've grown the economy 75  and at the same time we've cut carbon  emissions by almost half so that shows  it's possible to do both things we can  become more prosperous as a country more  jobs more successful businesses more  money in our pockets whilst also  becoming greener and that's what we need  to do going forward as well certainly  though anna this letter from nicholas  sturgeon to boris johnson asking him to  reassess the decision on cambod does  palm more pressure on him especially in  advance of that cop 26 climate  conference in glasgow certainly that  event has meant there is far more  scrutiny on our political leaders when  they make these sorts of decisions  joe thank you  well we've heard a lot about the  challenges of tackling climate change so  let's hear now from people coming up  with smart solutions a team of british  engineers are growing artificial rocks  in the gulf of mexico to slo